	// GetTransactionV2WithResponse Get an array of transactions
	//
	// Get all transactions for a client. Result can be limited with the search filter criteria.
	//
	// <b>Filter</b>
	// Filters can be added as query parameters by adding a question mark (?) at the end of the URL and then separate different filters with ampersands (&). Available filters can be found below in the Parameters-section.
	// <u>Example</u>: payroll.24sevenoffice.com/api/transaction/v2?payrollrunId=1&empId=10&serialNo=1
	//
	// Description of fields:<ul><li><b>empId</b> (ansattnr) employee number</li><li><b>serialNo</b> internal ID of the transaction. Serial numbers are unique per employee. Can be empty if the transaction is generated by the system (for example tax calculation).</li><li><b>payrollcode</b> (lønnsartkode) code to identify the wage type of the transaction</li><li><b>description</b> (beskrivelse) transaction description</li><li><b>payrollrunIds</b> (lønnskjøringsnummer) array of IDs of the payroll runs the transaction is connected to. Can be empty if transaction has not been included on a payroll run and can be multiple IDs if it is a repeating transaction.</li><li><b>datefrom</b> start date of the transaction. Format YYYY-MM-DD</li><li><b>dateto</b> end date of the transaction. Can be empty if it is a repeating transaction. Format YYYY-MM-DD</li><li><b>counts</b> (antall) count used on the transaction</li><li><b>unitprice</b> (sats) unit price used on the transaction</li><li><b>text</b> (fritekst) custom text on the post</li><li><b>note</b> (notat) custom internal text on the transaction</li><li><b>extent</b> (prosent) extent of the transaction</li><li><b>department</b> (avdeling) which department this transaction will be connected to</li><li><b>project</b> (prosjekt) which project this transaction will be connected to</li><li><b>tax</b> (trekk) the tax basis of the transaction. Available values are:<ul><li><b>0</b> - no tax</li><li><b>1</b> - table tax</li><li><b>2</b> - percentage tax</li><li><b>3</b> - border tax (grensegjenger)</li><li><b>4</b> - not tax calculated, A02 tax</li></ul></li><li><b>social_security</b> (AGA) boolean value determining if social security is calculated for the transaction</li><li><b>benefit</b> (fordel) benefit of the transaction reported in A-melding (A02). Available values are:<ul><b><li>kontantytelse</li><li>naturalytelse</li><li>utgiftsgodtgjoerelse</li></b></ul><li><b>is_paid</b> (utbetales) boolean value if the transaction is paid out</li><li><b>vacation</b> (ferie) type of vacation calculation for the transaction. Available values are:<ul><li><b>-1</b> - vacation withdrawal</li><li><b>0</b> - not basis for vacation</li><li><b>1</b> - basis for vacation</li></ul></li><li><b>wage_description</b> (lønnbeskrivelse) wage description of transaction reported in A-melding (A02)</li><li><b>earning_country</b> (opptjeningsland) country code of where the transaction was earned</li><li><b>tax_rule</b> (skatte- og avgiftsregel) tax rule reported in A-melding</li><li><b>repeating</b> (fast lønnspost) boolean value if the transaction is a repeating transaction. A repeating transaction either has no end date or the difference between the start date and the end date is more than a month.</li><li><b>first_60_days</b> (lønn første 60 dager) boolean value. Reported in A-melding whether a transaction is earned within the first 60 days. Only relevant if the transaction is earned on the continental shelf in Norway and the employee is tax resident in the USA.</li></ul>
